1
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:16,697
o ISBN Pierre

2
00:01:33,640 --> 00:01:37,720
To the sea where my father
is, the future Bonnie chooses!

3
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:51,570
Oh gross!

4
00:01:54,660 --> 00:01:55,920
Now come Kuma!

5
00:02:03,720 --> 00:02:04,600
Battle!

6
00:02:18,040 --> 00:02:19,440
Ahhhh!

7
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,720
Well, how'd you like that one?

8
00:02:25,820 --> 00:02:28,702
Don't worry, I'm not going
to use it on you guys.

9
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,020
I'm ready.

10
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:33,435
With moves like these, no
one in the world can beat me.

11
00:02:36,620 --> 00:02:38,760
I bet I could even take ace.

12
00:02:39,680 --> 00:02:40,510
Dragon.

13
00:02:50,120 --> 00:02:52,649
You seem rather familiar
with this country.

14
00:02:53,080 --> 00:02:56,786
Why did you go to that village
on its outskirts to see someone?

15
00:02:57,180 --> 00:03:00,768
You were watching that boy, but
you never said a word to him.

16
00:03:07,940 --> 00:03:10,411
Keep talking and it'll be the death of me.

17
00:03:12,140 --> 00:03:13,040
Why is that?

18
00:03:16,040 --> 00:03:19,560
A child is every parent's weak spot.

19
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,780
Sorry, I'll let it go.

20
00:03:25,340 --> 00:03:26,180
Forgive me.

21
00:03:32,540 --> 00:03:33,997
It's my special move!

22
00:03:34,080 --> 00:03:36,220
No one can stand up to that one!

23
00:03:37,900 --> 00:03:38,917
It's a big deal.

24
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:41,717
So I'll save it for when I gotta
fight someone really tough.

25
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:44,297
When I'm a pirate, I'm going
to have a crew, of course.

26
00:03:44,380 --> 00:03:47,277
But one of them might get beaten
up and captured by the enemy.

27
00:03:47,360 --> 00:03:49,480
Then I'll say, not so fast, jerk.

28
00:03:50,860 --> 00:03:52,780
Nobody messes with my crew.

29
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:55,800
So come go, battle axe. Huh?

30
00:03:58,020 --> 00:03:58,980
Still scared?

31
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:00,797
It's OK, guys.

32
00:04:00,880 --> 00:04:02,056
I don't eat cowards.

33
00:04:09,140 --> 00:04:10,320
Hey, who's there?

34
00:04:17,960 --> 00:04:19,940
It was weird. I felt something.

35
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,320
It gave me a chill.

36
00:04:24,440 --> 00:04:27,734
Some wild animal must be king
of the mountain here, huh?

37
00:04:28,320 --> 00:04:29,440
I'll find him.

38
00:04:39,880 --> 00:04:41,837
Pirates attacked a merchant ship and fled.

39
00:04:41,920 --> 00:04:44,038
Chase them down while they're close.

40
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,010
Who are you?

41
00:04:48,240 --> 00:04:49,475
I'm here to help you.

42
00:04:49,560 --> 00:04:52,357
Are you the merchants who were
raided by pirates just now?

43
00:04:52,440 --> 00:04:54,737
They showed up out of
nowhere and took our cargo.

44
00:04:54,820 --> 00:04:56,597
And can you take care of the fire?

45
00:04:56,680 --> 00:04:59,357
It looks bad, but we can
handle it, no problem.

46
00:04:59,440 --> 00:05:01,260
I'm not gonna make it.

47
00:05:01,460 --> 00:05:03,820
Please don't say that. Hang in there.

48
00:05:08,840 --> 00:05:09,670
Wait here.

49
00:05:09,753 --> 00:05:11,377
I'll transport him to a hospital.

50
00:05:11,460 --> 00:05:12,872
Hurry up and move, Kuma!

51
00:05:13,040 --> 00:05:14,037
What are you doing?

52
00:05:14,120 --> 00:05:15,617
Chase down that pirate ship!

53
00:05:15,700 --> 00:05:18,637
I'll have your cargo back
by the time you catch up.

54
00:05:18,720 --> 00:05:20,840
We'll be on our way soon. Thank you.

55
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:22,180
You're a hero.

56
00:05:28,280 --> 00:05:29,177
No! No!

57
00:05:29,260 --> 00:05:30,672
It's Bartholomew Goomba!

58
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:34,060
Surrender immediately. Aye aye, sir!

59
00:05:34,360 --> 00:05:37,301
Grab the cargo and bring
it in before he kills us!

60
00:05:41,660 --> 00:05:42,780
Dear Bonnie...

61
00:05:48,060 --> 00:05:53,840
The world's beauty can't be captured by
drawings or photos and encyclopedias.

62
00:06:02,520 --> 00:06:04,900
It's brimming with wonder at every turn.

63
00:06:06,820 --> 00:06:10,540
I can't wait to watch your
face light up when you see it.

64
00:06:30,280 --> 00:06:34,940
I'm sure your dad is just busy traveling,
or maybe the news coup got lost.

65
00:06:35,120 --> 00:06:38,277
But he said he'd write me, and
I haven't gotten one letter.

66
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:41,200
The more you want them,
the slower time will go.

67
00:06:42,780 --> 00:06:43,960
Be patient, dear.

68
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:45,631
They'll come soon enough.

69
00:06:46,300 --> 00:06:47,130
Oh.

70
00:06:47,760 --> 00:06:48,590
Oh!

71
00:06:50,760 --> 00:06:51,590
Hello?

72
00:06:56,480 --> 00:06:57,360
The newspaper.

73
00:06:57,820 --> 00:06:59,080
And a letter.

74
00:07:01,380 --> 00:07:02,757
Put this in the mailbox.

75
00:07:02,840 --> 00:07:03,670
Yes, ma 'am.

76
00:07:07,680 --> 00:07:08,510
A letter?

77
00:07:08,593 --> 00:07:09,740
No, sorry.

78
00:07:09,960 --> 00:07:11,340
It's just the paper.

79
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,377
Another letter came today.

80
00:07:20,460 --> 00:07:21,290
Yes.

81
00:07:21,373 --> 00:07:22,877
How many are we up to?

82
00:07:22,960 --> 00:07:25,517
He's been sending her
about 10 letters a month.

83
00:07:25,600 --> 00:07:27,137
It's been dozens by now.

84
00:07:27,220 --> 00:07:33,980
How can one idiot have
so much to write about?

85
00:07:37,140 --> 00:07:37,980
Dear Bonnie.

86
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:43,820
Get the shit!

87
00:07:46,380 --> 00:07:53,220
And Bonnie, though I've said
it countless times, I love you.

88
00:07:57,100 --> 00:07:59,280
All right, Pert, your turn.

89
00:08:00,360 --> 00:08:01,620
What's wrong, Bonnie?

90
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:03,070
Kyokyo?

91
00:08:05,200 --> 00:08:06,030
Mommy!

92
00:08:06,160 --> 00:08:07,680
Oh, come on, not again.

93
00:08:08,440 --> 00:08:10,680
Hey, want to play Jango? No!

94
00:08:10,940 --> 00:08:12,220
I want to play!

95
00:08:20,840 --> 00:08:22,580
You little freak!

96
00:08:27,220 --> 00:08:29,780
Bonnie, turn back to normal. Hurry!

97
00:08:30,820 --> 00:08:33,180
It's time to take your medicine, Bonnie.

98
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:39,237
She's so lucky to have a
hard-working nurse like you.

99
00:08:39,320 --> 00:08:40,614
Care for a cup of tea?

100
00:08:40,860 --> 00:08:41,717
No, I'm...

101
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:42,976
I'm fine, thank you.

102
00:08:45,060 --> 00:08:46,057
That's strange.

103
00:08:46,140 --> 00:08:47,480
Was I seeing things?

104
00:08:47,900 --> 00:08:50,606
Bonnie looked like some
sort of hulking brute.

105
00:08:56,360 --> 00:08:58,160
Here, open wide!

106
00:08:59,440 --> 00:09:01,737
Whoa, it's all better! I hate it!

107
00:09:01,820 --> 00:09:04,540
I know, sweetie, but it's good for you.

108
00:09:05,120 --> 00:09:07,296
Actually, it's just a bitter placebo.

109
00:09:07,440 --> 00:09:08,760
I'm confused, Connie.

110
00:09:09,020 --> 00:09:12,137
Why do we have to keep Bonnie's
powers a secret from her?

111
00:09:12,220 --> 00:09:13,820
Better to be safe, I say.

112
00:09:14,120 --> 00:09:17,649
Besides, haven't you heard that
a wise wolf hides its fangs?

113
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,457
That's incredible, doctor!

114
00:09:31,540 --> 00:09:32,797
It's complete already!

115
00:09:32,880 --> 00:09:37,837
Indeed, all that's left is to lift my
lab and my brain with island clouds.

116
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:40,817
Most of the buildings you
see here are holograms.

117
00:09:40,900 --> 00:09:45,537
I had intended to do on Punk Hassled
originally, like the head cut.

118
00:09:45,620 --> 00:09:49,957
By the way, I feel so light.

119
00:09:50,040 --> 00:09:51,275
I could don't for me.

120
00:09:56,360 --> 00:09:57,317
Poor Puma.

121
00:09:57,400 --> 00:09:59,997
They're really going to
take your free will away.

122
00:10:00,080 --> 00:10:02,437
Hmm.

123
00:10:02,520 --> 00:10:05,477
A clone with free will
and a human without it.

124
00:10:05,560 --> 00:10:07,457
Which one of us has it worse?

125
00:10:07,540 --> 00:10:10,317
Don't say that.

126
00:10:10,400 --> 00:10:12,297
To see, you're perfectly human.

127
00:10:12,380 --> 00:10:15,997
So when I lose my will,
what will that mean?

128
00:10:16,080 --> 00:10:19,597
Well, for example, you
say you follow orders now.

129
00:10:19,680 --> 00:10:22,777
But what if the government
ordered you to kill a child?

130
00:10:22,860 --> 00:10:24,660
You would resist. Yes.

131
00:10:25,960 --> 00:10:29,937
This experiment will strip side
away your memories as a human,

132
00:10:30,020 --> 00:10:32,314
and thus your human emotions will no...

133
00:10:32,920 --> 00:10:33,750
longer exist.

134
00:10:33,833 --> 00:10:35,400
The exam is done.

135
00:10:35,740 --> 00:10:38,140
You're free to go now. Looking good.

136
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:50,920
What's it like?

137
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,537
Starting to feel anxious?

138
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,450
I'm fine.

139
00:10:53,533 --> 00:10:55,117
I'm not worried about myself.

140
00:10:55,200 --> 00:10:56,030
I

141
00:10:56,680 --> 00:10:58,117
don't believe that for an instant.

142
00:10:58,200 --> 00:10:59,877
You'll lose your memories and emotions.

143
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:02,140
No one can simply accept that.

144
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,440
You couldn't.

145
00:11:03,640 --> 00:11:05,640
Not when there's someone you love.

146
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:12,122
Remember, until this is over, I'll ensure
that you retain some free fare, at least.

147
00:11:15,320 --> 00:11:18,340
You have roughly a year
till then, so don't worry.

148
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,348
Writing her another letter?

149
00:11:27,500 --> 00:11:30,441
I have to send as many as
I can while I have time.

150
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,329
To tell Bonnie I love her.

151
00:11:33,240 --> 00:11:37,537
Over the next year, I'm going to write
down a lifetime's worth of feelings.

152
00:11:37,620 --> 00:11:38,780
That's so sweet.

153
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:41,957
I can't believe she's
about to turn nine already.

154
00:11:42,040 --> 00:11:44,060
I bet she's grown so much.

155
00:11:44,480 --> 00:11:46,220
It hasn't been that long.

156
00:11:48,220 --> 00:11:51,097
I don't know when this letter
will reach you, Bonnie.

157
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,480
But happy ninth birthday.

158
00:11:53,940 --> 00:11:56,040
I'm at Vegapunk's lab right now.

159
00:11:56,980 --> 00:11:57,810
And...

160
00:12:00,660 --> 00:12:03,417
Mommy, happy birthday!

161
00:12:03,500 --> 00:12:05,257
We love you.

162
00:12:05,340 --> 00:12:11,037
Grandma, Connie made her special
giant pizza for you! Yay!

163
00:12:11,120 --> 00:12:12,040
Thank you!

164
00:12:17,200 --> 00:12:18,880
So good?

165
00:12:50,420 --> 00:12:51,250
Nothing.

166
00:12:51,600 --> 00:12:52,860
Still no letter.

167
00:12:54,020 --> 00:12:55,640
Be patient, dear.

168
00:12:55,840 --> 00:12:57,311
They'll come soon enough.

169
00:13:01,580 --> 00:13:04,240
It was my birthday today.

170
00:13:09,060 --> 00:13:14,260
Dad, you promised you'd write me.

171
00:13:38,660 --> 00:13:41,597
So kuma saved our forces again. Yes sir.

172
00:13:41,680 --> 00:13:44,268
We were in a bad spot
till he bailed us out.

173
00:13:48,640 --> 00:13:49,470
Kuma

174
00:13:51,400 --> 00:13:53,217
But he left without saying a word.

175
00:13:53,300 --> 00:13:54,300
Just like before.

176
00:13:55,620 --> 00:13:59,357
If that's what he wants
then fine let him go.

177
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,560
He must have a reason for it.

178
00:14:01,920 --> 00:14:03,720
One that he can't tell us.

179
00:14:08,760 --> 00:14:10,860
I'm killed! See? See?

180
00:14:11,160 --> 00:14:12,572
All the stones are gone!

181
00:14:14,300 --> 00:14:15,820
Oh, I'm so happy for you.

182
00:14:18,480 --> 00:14:20,960
You've been a very patient girl.

183
00:14:21,300 --> 00:14:23,240
I can go outside now!

184
00:14:24,300 --> 00:14:25,320
Not so fast.

185
00:14:26,360 --> 00:14:27,880
I'm still here.

186
00:14:30,920 --> 00:14:34,297
I'm supposed to take care of
you until your 10th birthday.

187
00:14:34,380 --> 00:14:36,556
And that's just what I'm going to do.

188
00:14:36,820 --> 00:14:37,680
You're a liar!

189
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:39,220
You can't trick me!

190
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:46,229
Vegapunk told me I'd be all better in
a year, and it's been longer than that!

191
00:14:46,620 --> 00:14:47,880
You can't leave.

192
00:14:49,180 --> 00:14:50,780
I'm not sick anymore!

193
00:14:50,940 --> 00:14:51,920
Leave me alone!

194
00:15:00,740 --> 00:15:02,900
Too bad for you.

195
00:15:08,140 --> 00:15:10,000
That nurse is terrible.

196
00:15:10,380 --> 00:15:12,086
How could she do this to her?

197
00:15:12,900 --> 00:15:14,360
I have news.

198
00:15:15,540 --> 00:15:19,160
Alpha and her teammates are
government intelligence agents.

199
00:15:20,960 --> 00:15:24,480
She's not a nurse, but
how can that Pass - Shhh!

200
00:15:27,720 --> 00:15:29,073
Here's what I've heard.

201
00:15:29,320 --> 00:15:33,980
She was getting drunk in town the
other day and kept running her mouth.

202
00:15:34,900 --> 00:15:36,841
Turns out you were right, Bonnie.

203
00:15:37,100 --> 00:15:39,820
She told people you were completely cured.

204
00:15:40,100 --> 00:15:41,140
She said that?

205
00:15:41,700 --> 00:15:45,780
I don't know what she's cooking up,
but it's too fishy for my taste.

206
00:15:46,040 --> 00:15:50,657
Why would she want to keep someone who's
perfectly healthy cooped up for six months?

207
00:15:50,740 --> 00:15:55,277
It's also strange that you haven't
gotten a single letter from Kuma,

208
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:56,480
don't you think?

209
00:16:03,240 --> 00:16:05,897
I've already talked with
Gyo-gyo and the others.

210
00:16:05,980 --> 00:16:07,297
Make for the port.

211
00:16:07,380 --> 00:16:09,697
Hurry, they'll take you to sea.

212
00:16:09,780 --> 00:16:11,597
And you can search for your father.

213
00:16:11,680 --> 00:16:13,151
You think we'll find him?

214
00:16:23,660 --> 00:16:25,040
Don't worry.

215
00:16:25,720 --> 00:16:27,480
You'll see him soon.

216
00:16:37,920 --> 00:16:39,060
You're leaving?

217
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:42,580
Yes, returning to the palace.

218
00:16:43,560 --> 00:16:44,860
Fine. Take care.

219
00:16:50,460 --> 00:16:53,520
Yokyo and his friends
are no ordinary fishable.

220
00:16:54,140 --> 00:16:58,180
Even pirates and sea monsters cower
at the mention of their names.

221
00:16:58,680 --> 00:17:02,120
With them on your side,
I know you'll find Kuma.

222
00:17:02,660 --> 00:17:04,160
I made it outside.

223
00:17:06,240 --> 00:17:07,220
There's dirt.

224
00:17:09,040 --> 00:17:10,200
And rain.

225
00:17:13,020 --> 00:17:14,580
The grass!

226
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:18,420
The sky!

227
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,180
The sun!

228
00:17:44,000 --> 00:17:46,320
Bonnie's actually walking outside.

229
00:17:46,860 --> 00:17:48,240
It's a miracle.

230
00:17:48,600 --> 00:17:50,020
There really is a god.

231
00:17:59,780 --> 00:18:02,100
I said sail!

232
00:18:10,100 --> 00:18:11,080
Bonnie!

233
00:18:11,500 --> 00:18:12,360
Over here!

234
00:18:13,020 --> 00:18:15,040
Yuckoo! Todd! Potato!

235
00:18:15,620 --> 00:18:16,720
Look! Look!

236
00:18:16,900 --> 00:18:18,220
I made it outside!

237
00:18:19,200 --> 00:18:20,720
Where's Bonnie hiding?

238
00:18:23,340 --> 00:18:25,120
Queen Dowager Connie?

239
00:18:25,440 --> 00:18:27,499
But you just went out a moment ago!

240
00:18:28,960 --> 00:18:30,680
What's going on here?

241
00:18:33,920 --> 00:18:34,980
I'm Bonnie!

242
00:18:35,200 --> 00:18:37,320
The hell you are! Neat, huh?

243
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:39,342
I made the ship look like pizza!

244
00:18:39,900 --> 00:18:41,320
I love it!

245
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:47,520
Fool me, will you?

246
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,060
You'll pay for this!

247
00:18:54,160 --> 00:18:56,660
And away we go!

248
00:18:58,880 --> 00:19:01,140
Not so fast!

249
00:19:01,920 --> 00:19:02,800
It's Alpha!

250
00:19:03,120 --> 00:19:04,080
We gotta move!

251
00:19:04,260 --> 00:19:05,140
She's coming!

252
00:19:07,660 --> 00:19:12,760
If the subject tries to escape, then
nothing is off the table anymore!

253
00:19:13,020 --> 00:19:15,780
I'll subdue you by any means necessary!

254
00:19:16,380 --> 00:19:19,560
That'll make this so much easier! What?

255
00:19:19,940 --> 00:19:21,600
She's a government agent!

256
00:19:21,740 --> 00:19:23,380
She uses the six powers!

257
00:19:23,740 --> 00:19:25,093
I can't keep going now.

258
00:19:25,620 --> 00:19:27,060
Not like this.

259
00:19:28,120 --> 00:19:30,000
I can't kill Bonnie.

260
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:32,400
But I can kill the rest!

261
00:19:33,660 --> 00:19:34,880
I can't.

262
00:19:35,220 --> 00:19:36,880
I can't go back.

263
00:19:38,220 --> 00:19:39,050
Dad.

264
00:19:39,920 --> 00:19:41,380
What should I do?

265
00:19:42,560 --> 00:19:45,500
Hey, Dad, can you tell
me what Nico looks like?

266
00:19:46,040 --> 00:19:49,640
Unfortunately, no one
knows for sure, but...

267
00:19:51,120 --> 00:19:51,950
Nico!

268
00:20:10,360 --> 00:20:11,640
DISTORTING Denjiro!

269
00:20:15,660 --> 00:20:16,860
You could transform!

